+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out, Filtering the Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. It declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. Its provenance stayed open, like every row the survey derived.
+
+A request to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty touched that row. Read broadly, the row covered any way of narrowing the directory, so the request could not proceed on implication.
+
+The owner decided the row on 2026-09-29, in the intake for the specialty filter.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the specialty filter as veterinarian search. Rejected by the owner.
+2. **Drop NG-9 for veterinarians.** Open free-text veterinarian search along with the filter. Rejected by the owner: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined. Filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's words, recorded at intake: "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+NG-9 keeps declining free-text search for pets, visits, and veterinarians. Narrowing the veterinarian directory to the veterinarians holding one attribute the directory already displays is not search under this row. The first such narrowing is the specialty filter.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation for veterinarians; the Non-Goals preamble names it decided. Its pet and visit clauses remain derived from absence.
+- Owner search stays the one demonstration of free-text search.
+- A filter on an attribute the directory does not show, or any free-text match on veterinarian names, stays declined. Opening either needs a recorded owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#veterinarian-directory) — the specialty filter the narrowing admits.
